  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given that,&nbsp;</p><p>Under the same reaction conditions, initial concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>386</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>dm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> of a substance becomes half in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>for&nbsp;first order and zero order kinetics, respectively.</p><p>For first order reaction,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>For zero order reaction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Divide eqn. (i) by (ii), we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mo>]</mo><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>693</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>386</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>dm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;</p>",
